  "calculus": "ZH",
  "fragment": "phase-free",
  "group": "zh-arithmetic",
  "order": 9,
  "summary": "An H-box with label 1 is the all-ones tensor, so it falls apart into phase-free Z-spiders.",
  "description": "An H-box with label $1$ has all its entries equal to $1$, so it is a product of the vectors $|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle$ on each leg: it disconnects into a phase-free arity-1 Z-spider on each of its legs.\n\nThis is frequently used after the [generalised multiply rule](../zh-multiply-generalised/): two standard H-boxes connected to the same Z-spiders multiply to an H-box with label $(-1)^2 = 1$, which then disappears.",
  "parameters": {
    "n": 1,
    "m": 2
  },
  "parameter_notes": "n inputs and m outputs on the H-box (shown for n = 1, m = 2); holds for any number of legs.",
